WEBVTT

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.940
<i>Tohtsuki {Tea House }Culinary Academy:{we didn't use "Tea House" in S1}</i>

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:12.900
<i>a culinary bastion that continues to produce world-renowned chefs.</i>

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.820
<i>Their high school first-years are contestants in the Autumn Selection,</i>

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.230
<i>which is now reaching its climax.</i>

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:23.040
<i>Those who have survived
 the preliminary round</i>

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:26.790
<i>are now preparing for the next battle.</i>

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:31.710
All right!

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:36.800
Did I pack the small knife?!

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:38.760
There it is!

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:43.010
Did I pack the timer?!

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.580
Today is just an explanation of the main tournament.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.350
Do you really need your tools?

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.440
Oh, right.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.060
Jeez. You never change.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.820
Hey, Tadokoro.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.680
Our ride's here.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.650
Let's go!

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.160
<i>The eight elites, all boasting impressive individuality and craftsmanship,</i>

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>will wear themselves to the bone 
to ascend to the top!</i>

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.980
<i>The Autumn Selection's main 
tournament is beginning!</i>

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.840
Souma-kun, based on the lottery results,

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:20.180
you'll be competing in the very first round.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.020
The theme for the round is bento.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.270
Bento?

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.770
You mean a boxed lunch?

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:26.350
That's right.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:30.060
You have the rest of the day to prepare for the match tomorrow.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.990
Bento, huh. This academy's more down-to-earth than I thought.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.740
What are you talking about?

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.570
You're ignorant to the extreme.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.370
Bento is a food culture unique to Japan.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:48.580
Gourmands have long loved bentos created from high-end seasonal ingredients.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.170
Even prominent chefs overseas 
are familiar with bentos,

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.710
and the word has even been added
 to a French dictionary.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:56.720
It is a highly appropriate theme
 for a celebration of food.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:01.220
It's an entirely different beast from the B-grade "gourmet" food that you're so skilled at!

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:04.850
Gotta say, I'm not a fan of 
that side of your personality.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:10.610
I'm pretty good at talking to people, 
but man, Nakiri, you're something else.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:11.360
What?!

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:14.730
Things were pretty tense between us on our way back from camp too!

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:15.990
What's your point?!

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.950
I have no idea what you're getting at!

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:20.110
You're irritating me!

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.450
Oh, this is odd.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.370
She doesn't usually raise her voice.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.040
Ah, I have a visitor regarding an unrelated topic.

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:27.870
Excuse me.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.830
Yukihira Souma.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:35.090
Try your best to make it through the rounds.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.220
It'd be quite a downer if you were to fail in the very first round.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.140
So... who am I going up against?

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.100
Thank you for your patience!

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.600
Welcome to the Autumn 
Selection's main tournament!

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.110
We will begin with 
the first match in round one!

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:01.910
Our first contestant is Candidate Yukihira Souma,
 who tied for second place in the Block A preliminaries.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:02.910
All right!

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.740
Good luck, Yukihira!

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:12.880
And his opponent is Candidate Nakiri Alice, who was the undisputed winner of the Block B preliminaries!

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.260
Nakiri Alice.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.760
<i>Granddaughter of the Academy 
Director, Nakiri Senzaemon,</i>

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.180
<i>and the grand champion of countless international competitions.</i>

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.640
<i>People call her the prodigy of molecular gastronomy.</i>

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:31.190
<i>Her curry dish, which received the highest score in the preliminaries,</i>

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:35.310
<i>made use of cutting-edge 
techniques and had a great impact.</i>

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.440
<i>How will you counter that, Yukihira?</i>

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:44.120
Yukihira-kun, today, I'll make your knees buckle with my cooking.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.160
Wow!

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.240
It's the latest in cooking equipment!

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:51.250
Even sitting in the audience,
 I can feel the tingling tension on my skin.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.540
I can't believe he has to face one of the Nakiris in this atmosphere.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:59.590
Yeah, I wonder how much pressure Yukihira is feeling right now.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:02.010
I deeply regret

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:06.550
that I'll only be able to see your cooking once on this great stage.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:10.890
If you lose, you can keep watching my cooking from the audience.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.640
Oh, I doubt that would ever happen.

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:17.230
Antiquated ideas and workmanship that rely on circus theatrics

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:19.610
are insufficient to best 
the limits of culinary knowledge.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:24.410
Oh, you didn't get a good night's rest?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.780
Oh, I was up pretty late testing my dish.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.580
It was dawn before I realized the time.

00:04:29.950 --> 00:04:31.700
But don't worry.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.000
This is just a normal day for me.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.750
Foodie customers with high expectations,{massive leadins on these three because it's preferrable to bleeds, and they'd be too fast otherwise}

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.710
shining knives honed to a razor edge,

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.420
and an array of ingredients...

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.800
The only thing that's different is that I have a formidable business rival in front of me.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:46.510
By beating you...

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.890
I'll gain a lot today.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.810
I'll use everything I gain 
to grow even stronger!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.440
On to the first match!

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.690
The topic is "bento."

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.520
The time limit is two hours!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:03.280
Let the cooking begin!

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.780
Good luck, Souma-kun.

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:17.500
It's like watching a chemistry experiment.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.000
Marui, explain!

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.880
No, this is beyond the limits of my knowledge.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:23.880
Are those glasses just for show?!

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:30.850
This makes my Japanese DNA very happy.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:36.390
What?

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:39.270
Oh, you were making fun 
of workmanship earlier,

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.570
but you <i>do</i> have skills.

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:41.690
Of course!

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:43.320
How rude!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.780
You shouldn't stare at people like that!

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:49.660
I remember being stared at during camp.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.160
He's up against the director's granddaughter.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.080
Damn it!

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:57.160
Yukihira, you'd better have 
some trick up your sleeve!

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.210
<i>I bet he can win.</i>

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.290
Finally!

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.880
It looks like both contestants 
are just about done!

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:06.130
Who will finish first?

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.630
It's Candidate Nakiri Alice!

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.100
Now, let's serve lunch.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.600
What?!

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.350
What <i>is</i> that?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:16.930
Is that mist under the transparent dome?

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.600
She's managed to make us wonder again!

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:23.070
Huh, there you go serving something weird again.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.320
What an excellent display. It piques one's interest.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.320
It is entirely befitting for a celebration of food.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:39.920
Temari sushi, is it?

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:40.880
Yes.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:44.750
I used every technique I had at my disposal to create this temari bento.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.380
It's so beautiful!

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.380
Hm, the mist was liquid nitrogen.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:54.640
It also had the purpose of keeping the sushi fresh with the chill, I assume.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.890
If I may,

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:00.060
I'd like to ask that you enjoy the contents in order, starting from the upper left.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.560
First, the bounties of the sea.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.070
There's mousse on top of the abalone.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:09.820
That mousse is kelp stock.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:12.700
The abalone was also wrapped
 in kelp during preparation.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.160
By wrapping abalone in kelp,

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.330
you can get rid of excess moisture and prolong its freshness.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.670
It's a method well-suited for making bento.

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:22.540
You're right.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:26.210
But I doubt that's the only reason for the kelp.

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.760
For that sushi,

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:32.470
I used bonito that has been aged for two days at low temperatures.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.510
Hm...

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.470
<i>The umami is out of this world!</i>

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.180
This umami isn't coming from the bonito alone.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.270
It's inosinic acid from the bonito

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.060
and glutamic acid from 
the kelp used in the first sushi.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.570
Those umami factors have a synergistic effect.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:51.740
This bento dish forms 
a complete picture in your mouth

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:55.070
as you eat each sushi in succession.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.120
Wow.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:57.160
I want to try that!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.040
It looks delicious.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.910
The second row is next.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:04.000
They are a type of sushi that uses vegetables called "sushi cakes" in some circles.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:06.000
Nori was not used in these sushi.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.050
Instead, paper-thin slices of vegetables are used to wrap the sushi.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:12.260
This bento has no use for heavy, dark colors.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.720
And finally, the third row.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.100
This practically screams, "I'm the main dish!"

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.180
It is aged beef fillet sushi.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.940
<i>Here comes another wave!</i>

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:29.400
<i>The two umami factors just 
spread through your mouth.</i>

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.320
I can see where the inosinic acid comes from, 
given that there's meat involved,

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.660
but what about the glutamic acid?

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:36.030
Tomatoes.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.410
Tomatoes?

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:38.950
I don't see them anywhere.

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.000
It was a component of the sushi cakes.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:48.000
I used a centrifuge to separate tomatoes into pigment, fiber, and jus.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.420
The jus was filtered several times 
to remove impurities.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:53.470
A few drops of that jus 
was added to the sushi cakes.

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.800
I see!

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:58.010
To think that the original ingredient was rendered completely invisible!

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.390
Now, the last item.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.850
What is the sphere nestled next 
to the sea bream sushi?

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.820
<i>The sphere...</i>

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:12.820
<i>is concentrated stock!</i>

00:09:13.490 --> 00:09:16.860
This is a sea bream chazuke that comes together on your tongue!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.450
<i>"The prodigy of molecular gastronomy."</i>

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.660
<i>Her technique does justice to her moniker.</i>

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.870
<i>She was able to entertain her guests with her cooking from start to finish.</i>

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.040
<i>This deep satisfaction</i>

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:34.010
<i>is as though we just enjoyed a feast at a luxurious traditional Japanese restaurant!</i>

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.430
This tiny bento box

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.930
roars forth such...

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:42.350
culinary wisdom!

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:43.470
He's bared his chest!

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:44.180
There he goes!

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.850
The director's gone bare-chested!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.520
Well done.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.230
This is Nakiri Alice's true strength.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:54.740
How can such a chef be the same age as us?

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.700
Even if I spent my entire life trying to reach her level, I never will...

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:02.080
When one's genius shines too 
brightly, it casts a shadow.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.790
That is her karma.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.830
This is Tohtsuki Academy.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:09.790
I have no need for weaklings 
who would falter from this display.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.250
Look.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.470
Five bentos, all done!

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:21.140
There's at least <i>one</i> chef who is not deterred.

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:24.350
Yukihira Souma, what is your dish?

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.310
Nori bento.

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.140
What?!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.270
Did he say nori bento?!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:29.770
What?!

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:33.020
How can he possibly hope 
to beat Nakiri Alice with that?

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:43.660
Nori bento?!

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:44.200
What the hell?

00:10:44.200 --> 00:10:44.950
He's finished.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:46.660
Yukihira-kun.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:47.910
Huh?

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.170
What's a nori bento?

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:52.540
What, you don't know?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:54.880
I can make one for you later.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.300
It's not just any nori bento, though.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.260
It's Yukihira-style Evolved Nori Bento!

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:02.970
Enjoy!

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:05.930
They're called lunch jars.

00:11:06.310 --> 00:11:11.350
They're made of stainless steel and can retain the heat of rice and soup.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:14.900
Hm? Japanese bento boxes are pretty advanced.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:19.030
More recent models can retain their contents' heat for up to half a day.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.320
If you heat up the soup before you put it in the jar,

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.490
it does a better job of keeping the rice warm.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:25.280
Oh, how clever!

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:26.990
Where's the tension?

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.870
It's not like the match is over.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.790
She's being condescending toward Yukihira.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:36.090
She's all smiles because she's convinced she'll win.

00:11:36.550 --> 00:11:40.670
Hm... First, there are three side dishes.

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.090
Hm!

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:46.810
This fish cake fried with nori is amazing!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:50.680
I made the fish cake from scratch.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.060
He used beer in the batter.

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:55.770
Alcohol is more volatile than the batter,

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:57.780
so it becomes light and crispy.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:58.400
Huh?

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.820
How do you know what he did, Ryouko?

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:03.820
I saw Yukihira-kun testing his dish at the dorm last night,

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.160
so I asked for a taste.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:08.240
<i>Oh!</i>

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.660
<i>So much umami's bursting forth!</i>

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.250
<i>I can smell the sea!</i>

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.420
<i>I'll envelop you.</i>

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:17.090
<i>Wh-Who are you?</i>

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:23.510
The kinpira-style sauteed burdock also has a mellow, deep flavor.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:27.970
I've added just a bit of mayonnaise and balsamic vinegar as secret ingredients.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.060
I see.

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:31.730
You were very meticulous with this dish.

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:32.600
Oh!

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:35.690
Look how easily the chopsticks 
cut through the fried cod!

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:40.610
The cod must've been first simmered in stock and seasoning before it was fried.

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:44.110
That step gave it its soft, flaky texture.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.950
What?!

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:55.120
What a pure, mild flavor it has!

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.420
It is like a gentle highlands breeze!

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:00.840
What refined flavor!

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.550
Where is this coming from?!

00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:05.720
The answer to that question 
can be found in the stock.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:09.470
This is dried tuna stock.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:10.890
That's right.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:14.730
The cod was simmered in stock made from dried tuna and rishiri kelp.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.690
Dried tuna...

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:19.690
That would've been made from yellowfin tuna.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.730
Yes.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:26.030
While it is not as rich as bonito stock,
 it has a very delicate and elegant umami.

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:30.870
Cod also has a light umami,
 so the dried tuna is a perfect match.

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.410
What a light dish!

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:35.370
The soup is next!

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:36.500
Oh!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:39.250
It's bacon and onion miso soup!

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.130
Ah, this too...

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:49.390
<i>The unique fragrance 
of the tuna stock fills your nostrils.</i>

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.680
<i>Combined with the meltingly sweet onions,</i>

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.730
<i>it's as though the soup envelops your entire body!</i>

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:00.810
Also, there is a trick 
to taking advantage of this bento box.

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:05.400
Just by putting the stock, ingredients, and seasonings in the container,

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:09.490
you can have a sweet soup a few hours later.
 The vegetables will be cooked through.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.950
Oh, that's useful.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.250
Today, there won't be any time delay,
 so I've cooked the ingredients already.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.710
You know a lot about bentos.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:22.090
Sure. I've made them at my family's diner.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:24.760
But that's not enough, Yukihira-kun.

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.420
Your efforts are all too conventional.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:31.220
Even bentos should be full 
of spectacular surprises.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:34.220
Just like my temari bento.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:37.940
Yeah, yours did look really tasty.

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.690
Let me try it sometime.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:41.810
Yes, of course.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:47.650
But was your dish really amazing as a bento?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.490
What did you say?

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.990
I'm asking you what we should
 be putting in bento boxes.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:59.670
One of my diner's regulars 
was a granny called Kiyo-san.

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:02.630
She came almost every day,

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:05.460
but one day, she hurt her back and couldn't come.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.220
<i>Hello?</i>

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:09.840
<i>Granny Kiyo!</i>

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.720
<i>Is your back okay?!</i>

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.930
<i>Souma-chan, isn't your diner busy right now?</i>

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.720
<i>Ow...</i>

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.180
<i>Here you go!</i>

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:19.270
<i>What?</i>

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.890
<i>You haven't had dinner yet, right?</i>

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:21.560
<i>Later!</i>

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:24.020
<i>You came here just to deliver this?</i>

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:28.690
<i>The diner was super empty, 
so I made this for you.</i>

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.700
<i>Eat it up and get better!</i>

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:36.700
<i>P.S: Lift up the nori before eating the rice!</i>

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:44.420
Now you're going to taste what 
I was trying to deliver...

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.210
in that bento box back then.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:50.340
The flavors...

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:52.550
and what lies beyond!

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.760
What?

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:56.430
What is this rice?

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:58.220
I-Is this...

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.430
...really nori bento?!

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:06.520
There are strange black grains on top of the rice.

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:07.480
What's that?

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.190
Caviar?

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:08.860
Salmon roe?

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:10.110
It's black.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:12.070
How curious!

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.280
Nonetheless, I must try this.

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.780
Knock on wood!

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:22.290
It feels like salmon roe 
bursting in your mouth!

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:26.590
What gushes forth 
from within is the umami of nori!

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:34.510
The nori's salty umami goodness bursts forth to coat each grain of rice.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:35.550
I can't stand it!

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:37.640
It's addicting!

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.180
You made those spheres 
by extracting the nori's umami

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:44.900
and adding sodium alginate 
and potassium chloride.

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:46.690
Molecular gastronomy!

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:47.560
But that's...

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.400
...Nakiri Alice's specialty!

00:16:49.400 --> 00:16:52.110
How do you know this technique?

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:57.700
The other day, Isshiki-senpai invited me to help out at a kids' cooking class.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.410
Huh?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:01.200
I got to be buddy-buddy with the kids.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.120
At the end of class, 
they gave me snacks and stuff.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.670
One of the snacks 
reminded me of something...

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:10.420
When I was a kid, I'd tried one of these.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:11.510
What?

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:12.590
A cheap candy product?!

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:14.800
What are you talking about?

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.680
This is one of those so-called educational snacks.

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:21.310
Potassium chloride and sodium alginate...

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.770
It's a snack that lets you make artificial fish roe.

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.600
I was really into it as a kid.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.270
I played around with it quite a bit.

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:29.400
<i>Look, Dad!</i>

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:30.690
<i>I made miso soup solid!</i>

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:32.990
<i>Wow, that's cool.</i>

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.240
<i>But don't ever serve that at our diner.</i>

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:39.070
These black beads are nori umami bombs

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:41.240
that I made from seasoned nori.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:46.420
He thought of a molecular gastronomy 
technique from a cheap candy product?

00:17:46.420 --> 00:17:47.250
Hm?

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:49.460
There's something else in the rice...

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.380
<i>So much flavor!</i>

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:56.010
It's dried tuna simmered down in soy sauce!

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.840
It was a four-layer dish!

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:04.560
If Nakiri Alice's dish was 
a meticulously-arranged jewel box,

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:10.360
this nori bento is a treasure box full of marvels waiting to be discovered!

00:18:10.770 --> 00:18:13.650
It reminds me of my field trips and picnics as a child.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:17.400
That excitement 
when I'd open the bento box...

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:20.320
It's all coming back to me now!

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:24.620
My temari bento even included a finishing dish: the sea bream chazuke!

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:27.210
The overall taste quality was higher in mine—

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:28.540
Oh, please stop!

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:31.630
Can you leave about one-third of the rice?

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:35.880
There's yet another compartment under the very first lid.

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:38.130
It's kudzu sauce!

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:43.560
That kudzu sauce has three times more dried tuna and rishiri kelp than normal.

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.930
Pour it over the piping hot rice and dig in.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:48.890
Let's finish up.

00:18:48.890 --> 00:18:50.480
Of course that's...

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.610
...going to be...

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:52.650
...going to be...

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:55.070
...delicious!

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.240
Ah, kudzu sauce!

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:59.030
It's so good!

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:01.280
Combined with the nori bombs...

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.660
...it's a whole new level of flavor!

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:06.080
Those judges...

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:08.540
They're eating like they're really having fun,

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.460
unlike when they were eating Nakiri Alice's dish.

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.340
Yukihira-kun.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:17.840
Are you trying to make the point that bentos should contain "heart"?

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.590
What's important is the flavor, isn't it?

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.050
Don't get all "mind over matter" on me—

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:22.760
No!

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:26.260
It's not about that, Alice.

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:27.140
Grandfather!

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:29.890
<i>When'd he get bare-chested?!</i>

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:35.150
Alice, your bento took advantage of the cold.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:38.110
Yes, because bentos should be chilled.

00:19:38.110 --> 00:19:42.530
Yukihira Souma didn't get fixated like that.

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:47.410
He first thought about the bento container,

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:51.830
then filled it with entertainment
 whose flavor was enhanced by warmth.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:54.500
That's what this bento is.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:58.550
Of course, your dish 
was delicious in the extreme.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:01.720
But wouldn't you say that you could've served the same dish

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:03.890
if the theme had been sushi?

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:09.180
You merely used your skills to fill that box.

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:12.480
There are flavors that can only be communicated through bento.

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:16.400
There are creative techniques you can devise to advance bento culture.

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.940
Bentos can be fun 
and innovative in their own way.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:22.860
Did your dish capture any of that?

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:25.700
Well, sure... but what's important is the flavor.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:28.030
I don't disagree with that.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.200
Dig in, Nakiri Alice!

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.430
<i>Alice-sama, you look well.</i>

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:48.310
<i>How is Erina-sama?</i>

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.430
<i>Please give Erina-sama my regards.</i>

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:51.060
<i>Erina-sama.</i>

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:51.930
<i>Erina-sama!</i>

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:52.390
<i>Erina-sama.</i>

00:20:52.390 --> 00:20:53.060
<i>Erina-sama!</i>

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:54.270
<i>Erina-sama...</i>

00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:59.650
<i>Father, I would like to go to
 your research lab in Scandinavia!</i>

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:02.530
<i>Please take me there now!</i>

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:05.570
<i>What's cutting-edge... the most advanced...</i>

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:09.370
<i>I must gain weapons that are mine alone, so that I won't lose to Erina.</i>

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:12.660
<i>I can't lose to anyone...</i>

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:15.420
<i>before I win against Erina, and yet...</i>

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.340
Bring me the brush!

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:47.110
It's so warm.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:52.450
Round one, match one!

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:53.450
The victor...

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:57.500
is Yukihira Souma!

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.330
Glad you liked it!

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:00.130
He won!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.800
Woohoo!

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:05.590
Yukihira!

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:06.930
Miss Alice...

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:13.060
Yukihira, you're really interesting.

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:37.710
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:44.170
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:47.920
An endless journey

00:22:47.920 --> 00:22:52.930
Let's hone each other's pride

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:55.430
Words aren't really important

00:22:55.430 --> 00:22:57.930
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:04.900
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:07.280
No reason

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:09.780
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:23:09.780 --> 00:23:12.530
We're reckless challengers

00:23:12.530 --> 00:23:17.540
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:20.080
A swordsman should use his blade

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:22.920
To open the way to the future

00:23:22.920 --> 00:23:28.630
This is my story and no one else's

00:23:44.360 --> 00:23:45.480
Souma-kun.

00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:46.400
Wow!

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:47.650
You're amazing!

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:49.820
The second match is about to begin.

00:23:49.820 --> 00:23:50.650
Please get ready.

00:23:50.650 --> 00:23:52.570
Oh, o-okay.

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:56.450
<i>It's my turn next!</i>

00:24:07.130 --> 00:24:11.050
Next time: The Interplay 
of Light and Shadow.
